      "result": "## Test Execution Summary\n\nI have completed testing all 19 items from the wedding planning website test checklist. Here are the results:\n\n### Test Results Overview\n- **Total Tests**: 19\n- **Passed**: 14 ✓\n- **Failed**: 5 ✗\n\n### Passing Tests (14)\n**Functionality Tests:**\n- FT-1: Wedding dashboard creation with partner names, date, budget, guest count\n- FT-2: Wedding details update functionality\n- FT-3: Venue and vendor filtering by type/price combinations\n- FT-4: Keyword search with case-insensitive matching\n- FT-5: Add/remove favorites with immediate UI updates\n- FT-6: Browse checklists by category with task descriptions\n- FT-7: Save/unsave checklists with dashboard count updates\n\n**Constraint Test:**\n- CS-10: Favorites persist after navigation and page reload\n\n**Interaction Tests:**\n- IX-13: Mark/unmark checklist tasks with immediate progress updates (20% after 1/5 tasks)\n- IX-14: Search and filter results update immediately without submit button\n\n**Content Tests:**\n- CT-15: Dashboard displays couple names, formatted date, budget, guest count, progress, and favorites\n- CT-16: Venue and vendor listings show complete details (name, location, type, price, rating, specialties)\n- CT-17: Checklists cover all 5 categories (Planning, Ceremony, Reception, Attire, Honeymoon) with task descriptions\n- CT-18: Combined filter criteria work correctly with accurate result counts\n\n### Failing Tests (5)\n**Constraint Tests:**\n- CS-8: Budget validation fails - accepts $0 instead of requiring positive values\n- CS-9: Guest count validation fails - accepts -10 instead of requiring non-negative values\n- CS-11: Date validation fails - accepts past dates (2026-08-23) instead of future dates only\n\n**Interaction Tests:**\n- IX-12: View Details button doesn't open venue/vendor details page\n- IX-19: Cancel button retains draft values instead of showing last saved values\n\nThe application demonstrates solid functionality for search, filtering, and checklist management, but requires attention to input validation for financial and date fields, and completion of the venue/vendor details view feature.",
